{title: From the Morning}
{artist: Nick Drake}

{define: DaddG frets 0 2 2 0}
{define: A7sus4 frets 0 1 0 0}
# Ukulele group practice sheet standard G-C-E-A tuning

# Chord diagrams: strings left to right GCE A; filled dots = fret, o = open string.

# Practice adaptation - chord-change timing NOT verified against Matt Stead's tutorial.

Verse 1
[DaddG]A day once [G]dawned, and it was [DaddG]beautiful [G]
[DaddG]A day once [G]dawned from the [A7sus4]ground [A7]
[DaddG]Then the night she [G]fell, and the [DaddG]air was beautiful [G]
[DaddG]The night she [G]fell all a[DaddG]round [G]

Refrain
[DaddG]So look, see the [A7sus4]days [A7]
[G]The endless coloured [DaddG]ways [G]
[DaddG]Go play the [G]game that you [A7sus4]learnt [A7]
From the [DaddG]morning [G]

Verse 2
[DaddG]And now we [G]rise, and we are [DaddG]everywhere [G]
[DaddG]And now we [G]rise from the [A7sus4]ground [A7]
[DaddG]And see she [G]flies, she is [DaddG]everywhere [G]
[DaddG]See she [G]flies all a[DaddG]round [G]

Refrain
[DaddG]So look, see the [A7sus4]sights [A7]
[G]The endless summer [DaddG]nights [G]
[DaddG]And go play the [G]game that you [A7sus4]learnt [A7]
